datasets, models, or service interfaces integrated with or utilized by SANGAM,
including but not limited to:

a) Mapping and Cartography:
   - MapLibre GL and @maplibre/maplibre-gl-leaflet (governed by their respective
     open-source licenses);
   - OpenFreeMap vector tile service and hosting infrastructure (governed by
     its applicable third-party terms and license);
   - OpenMapTiles vector cartographic schema and data (CC-BY 4.0);
   - OpenStreetMap spatial and geographic data (Open Data Commons Open Database
     License - ODbL); and
   - DataMeet India national boundary dataset (Creative Commons Zero 1.0
     Universal - CC0 Public Domain Dedication; see boundary provenance in
     frontend/public/data/BOUNDARIES.md).

b) Meteorological Models, Services, and Data Providers:
   - European Centre for Medium-Range Weather Forecasts (ECMWF) IFS, AIFS,
     and ERA5 Atmospheric Reanalysis data and services;
   - National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA) / NCEP GFS data;
   - Deutscher Wetterdienst (DWD) ICON model data;
   - Open-Meteo weather API services; and
   - Bharat Forecast System (BharatFS) and Mission Mausam materials developed
     by IITM Pune, IMD, and NCMRWF (Ministry of Earth Sciences, Govt. of India).

c) Third-Party Software and Libraries:
   - Python packages, runtime modules, and machine-learning libraries (FastAPI,
     LightGBM, Pydantic, NumPy, SciPy, Pytest, Uvicorn, etc.);
   - JavaScript/TypeScript dependencies (React, Vite, Leaflet, Lucide, etc.); and
   - Any other external models, APIs, packages, or assets.

